    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Occasional North American Monsoon storms bring brief thunderstorms to Golden Valley, adding a touch of moisture to its otherwise dry climate.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/golden_valley_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the Northern Paiute hunted and gathered in Golden Valley, leaving archaeological traces across the Truckee Meadows.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/golden_valley_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1869 completion of the transcontinental railroad opened Golden Valley to California, accelerating settlement in the Reno area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/golden_valley_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Golden Valley sits 7 mi north of downtown Reno, covering 3.6 sq mi in the Sierra Nevada foothills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/golden_valley_nevada"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Sagebrush steppe dominates Golden Valley’s landscape, supporting mule deer and golden eagles amid scattered piñon‑juniper woodlands.",
